Reliability
-----------

[ ] Verify the base image checksum after download
    File:  scripts/lib/cloudinit.sh (cloudinit_fetch_base_image)
    Why:   A partial download or a corrupted file will produce broken VMs with
           no clear error message. Debian publishes a SHA256SUMS file alongside
           each cloud image.
    How:   After wget completes, download the corresponding SHA256SUMS file
           from the same URL directory and run 'sha256sum --check' against the
           downloaded image. Delete the image and exit with an error if the
           check fails.
    Skill: bash, wget, sha256sum

[ ] Make the base image download resumable
    File:  scripts/lib/cloudinit.sh (cloudinit_fetch_base_image)
    Why:   The Debian base image is ~400 MB. If the download is interrupted,
           the script currently restarts from zero on the next run.
    How:   Add '--continue' to the wget call so partial downloads are resumed.
           Also add '--tries=3' for automatic retry on transient failures.
    Skill: bash, wget

[ ] Warn when the base image backing path is no longer valid
    File:  scripts/lib/cloudinit.sh (cloudinit_create_overlay) or
           scripts/create_vm.sh
    Why:   qemu-img stores the base image as an absolute path inside the
           overlay. If the base image is moved or renamed after the overlay
           was created, QEMU fails at boot with a cryptic error.
    How:   Before launching QEMU, use 'qemu-img info --output=json <overlay>'
           to extract the backing file path and check that it still exists.
           Print a clear error with the missing path if it does not.
    Skill: bash, qemu-img, JSON parsing (jq or grep)

